		"abstractNote": "Social concordance is a facilitator of key dimensions of healthcare engagement and may mitigate effects of systemic oppression. Given social hierarchies disadvantage marginalized patients in medical encounters, social concordance can strengthen the patient-clinician therapeutic alliance and increase communication and epistemic justice, necessary precursors to patient empowerment and improved health outcomes.",
